# The container's schedule, run by supercronic (see Dockerfile).
#
# CRON_TZ pins the scans to the market's clock, so they stay at the same point in the session
# whatever TZ the container shows in its logs, and across the daylight-saving change. Two scans a
# weekday: an hour after the open and an hour before the close. Each saves its whole ranked result
# to /data/runs, which is the log `validate` needs, then rebuilds the report and publishes it. A
# spread listed on both runs counts once, at its first listing. Edit an expression and rebuild.
#
# There is no holiday calendar. A scan on a market holiday runs against the last session's quotes
# and saves a run that repeats the day before; harmless to `validate`, but the published report
# will say it ran.
#
# The 15-minute line is only the heartbeat the healthcheck reads (healthcheck.sh): the scans are
# too far apart for their own timestamp to say the scheduler is alive.
CRON_TZ=America/New_York
*/15 * * * * touch /tmp/alive
0 10,15 * * 1-5 /app/docker/run-scan.sh
